# Shell scripts that CI executes must keep LF line endings. A script committed
# with CRLF fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and the failure
# looks like a broken scanner rather than a line-ending problem.
#
# Scoped to the CI scripts directory on purpose: a repository-wide `*.sh` rule
# would renormalise the existing benchmark scripts and show them as modified in
# working copies that currently have CRLF checked out.
/.github/scripts/*.sh text eol=lf

# The Step 4A/4B tenancy artifacts are compared byte-for-byte against generated
# output. On Windows, core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to CRLF on checkout while
# the generator emits LF, so a fresh clone fails a test that CI passes. Pinning
# them to LF makes the comparison mean the same thing on every platform.
/docs/tenancy/*.json text eol=lf
/docs/tenancy/*.md   text eol=lf
